Serial functions:
When your computer sends data to the Arduino, the incoming bytes are stored in a temporary memory location called a buffer. The buffer can hold up to 64 bytes.

Serial.available()
Before you read data, you must check if any data has actually arrived. This function returns the number of bytes waiting in the buffer.
Serial.read():
Reads the oldest single byte waiting in the buffer. Once read, that byte is removed from the buffer.

Serial.read() will only get one character per time. To get full number at once -> integer or float we use these two functions: Serial.parseInt(), Serial.parseFloat()
